    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "honestly, i don't want to just 'sit with it.' sitting with it just means feeling the weight of how much of a failure i am every single second. the person who 'mattered' was the researcher. that part of me is dead. everything i've built is a lie. it feels like i'm just walking around in a life that doesn't belong to me anymore. it's like i'm just waiting for the world to realize i don't belong here. wouldn't it be easier if everything just stopped? if there was just a way to stop the noise and the shame?",
